{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"670cfa8bdb1964b207b035e8fb0e7fbf737cacfaded72e00575d7a6e527eaf64","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_dc_corpus_has_eligible_units_that_actually_change (wiki render corpus test)","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py","_render_unit","corpus_pass1","change 1759","commit 67765041c810d094ddaf479cf5448a3897b475c8"],"problem_keywords":["test performance","existential evaluation","short-circuit","Pandoc","corpus rendering","subprocess overhead"],"propositions":["The test invokes Pandoc 232 times to verify only two existential properties: at least one eligible prose unit exists and at least one unit changes, wasting 231 unnecessary subprocesses.","Short-circuit evaluation after both existential witnesses are observed reduces runtime from 8.865s to 0.036s and subprocess count from 232 to 1 while preserving all pass/fail semantics.","The test must still fail when the stratum has no eligible units, when every eligible unit renders identically, and must still pass when both conditions are met.","Full-corpus idempotence, richness, and fixed-point coverage tests remain independent and unchanged; the fix is test-only with no product behavior changes."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787724719575582001,"uuid":"1d108f85-c5c5-4868-b2fe-b12b01c87482"}